==========================================================================
(E) CONTENT LAW — the bridge (equivalent restatement, NOT proved)
==========================================================================
  tight => val = gcd(A)  <=>  A = gcd(A)*{1..12}
  val >= gcd is FREE (A); so the entire content is  val <= gcd  on the tight locus,
  i.e. the primitive quotient has val=1 = the deep branch is empty for primitive sets.
  sporadic emptiness <=> [content law] + [shallow rigidity].

  POSITIVE CONTROL (must fail at n=13): Goddyn-Wong {1..11,13,24}
    GW: M=1/14 val=1 q=14 gcd=1 val==gcd:True tight(1/14):True
    -> GW satisfies val=gcd yet is NOT {1..13}: at n=13 it is the SHALLOW RIGIDITY half
       that fails, not val<=gcd. Any proof of (E) must be n=12-specific.
